differential2 §11b residual: custom data descriptors. PLR: accessing a
class attribute bound to a descriptor instance calls its __get__, so
c.d == 42. CBMC does not recognise a class-level descriptor instance
(it is not typed as the descriptor class) and does not dispatch
__get__/__set__, so the assertion cannot be established. The KNOWNBUG
regex states the PLR-correct outcome. @property (the built-in data
descriptor) is supported; user-defined descriptors need the descriptor
protocol over instance-dict storage.
